WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:12.056
Now the fun part: your wallet. Have your phone, your hardware wallet, and your guardian's page at hand.

2
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:22.254
First, open Trikey and pick the network. For testing, choose Signet: its coins have no value. Then tap Create a wallet.

3
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:32.272
Connect your hardware wallet. A Ledger needs its Bitcoin Test app open; a Trezor works through Suite Lite.

4
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:45.471
Next, add an alert contact: a nostr account that hears about anything unusual. On a test network you can skip it, but it's worth doing.

5
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:57.944
On your guardian's page, make a pairing code, and scan it with the app. They talk over encrypted messages, so nothing on your network is opened.

6
00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:10.024
Your daily limit matters. Payments under it need just your phone. Anything bigger needs your hardware wallet.

7
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:18.049
Choose your daily limit, and the waiting period for recoveries. Then approve the rules on your hardware wallet.

8
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:31.321
Last, back up this phone. Write the recovery code on paper, and save the backup file somewhere that isn't this phone. Keep the two apart.

9
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:42.116
That's your wallet. Next, let's receive and send some coins.
